  "notes": [
    "Minimum of one Line Infantry Brigade per 500 points. A brigade has 1-2 German or Hungarian Line Infantry Regiments of up to 2 Large battalions (cannot have more Hungarian than German regiments).",
    "A Line Infantry Brigade may add up to two of: Grenadier battalions, Large Grenz battalions (max 1 per 4 infantry battalions), or a 6-pdr Brigade battery.",
    "Up to 1 Light Cavalry Brigade: 1-2 Large Hussar/Chevauleger regiments, plus an optional Dragoon regiment and a cavalry battery (1 per 3 cavalry regiments).",
    "Up to 1 Advanced Guard Brigade: up to 6 infantry battalions/cavalry regiments (Jäger, Line, Grenz, Hussar, Dragoon, Large Uhlan/Chevauleger, plus a battery) — infantry battalions must equal or exceed cavalry regiments.",
    "Reserves: up to 25% of points on Abteilung and Army Support, including Reserve Artillery (1 Position battery per 9 line infantry battalions).",
    "0 to 1 Grenadier Brigade and 0 to 1 Heavy Cavalry Brigade are included for completeness, although not part of the campaign.",
    "Cavalry note: Austrian regiments fought as two-squadron Abteilungen — a regiment may be replaced by 2, 3 or 4 Small units at 8 points per squadron-sized reduction step (standard unit price).",
    "Allies: an Austrian army can take 25% allies from the French or Confederation States Saxon list."
  ]
